LAMMPS accelerator list (admin task)
====================================

The "Filter results by" hardware checkboxes list ../accelerators/<cluster>.json, one file per
cluster. utils.py reads the same file: "vendor" decides whether the NVML GPU monitor runs
(nvidia only), "constraints" maps a GPU count to a Slurm --constraint (e.g. PVC Xe Link).
An optional "counts" list, e.g. "counts": [1, 2, 4, 8], limits the GPU counts users can request
for that type: the create form shows a dropdown with those values instead of a number field
(ACES PVC: 1, 2, 4 or 8 only). The generator never adds it; set it by hand.
The form only reads the file; it never runs sinfo.

Build or refresh it on each cluster where the environment is offered, and again after GPU
types are added or removed there:

  ./generate_accelerators.py            # writes ../accelerators/<cluster>.json
  ./generate_accelerators.py -n         # dry run: print the list, write nothing

It takes the GPU types from Slurm (sinfo GRES) and adds CPU. Every GPU type is listed, also
one the LAMMPS validator has no builds for yet (checking only that type then shows no
strategies). Options:
  --require-build   leave out GPU types the validator (/sw/hprc/sw/lammps-validator,
                    --validator) has no builds for
  --exclude ve      leave types out
  --cluster NAME    default: DRONA_CLUSTER, else Slurm ClusterName

You may edit label, vendor, constraints and counts in the file by hand; a re-run keeps them for
types it finds again, adds new types and drops types that are gone (it prints what it did).
Unknown type names get vendor "unknown" and a warning: set nvidia, intel or amd.

Without a file for a cluster the filter only offers CPU. utils.py then falls back to the
rules of the 1.x environment (h100/a30 NVIDIA, PVC xelink2/xelink4).
